WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:02.720
Look out! Here come the Spider-Men.

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:07.440
"Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse" was the first&nbsp;
theatrical movie to crack open the concept of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:12.720
multiverse for Spider-Man. The MCU's live-action&nbsp;
"Spider-Man: No Way Home" is following in those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:18.000
footsteps in a lot of ways, bringing in characters&nbsp;
from other universes — bad guys, and good guys.&nbsp;

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:22.240
Alright, let's get this out of the way&nbsp;
— yes, Andrew Garfield and Tobey Maguire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:25.680
are in this movie in the roles of&nbsp;
Peter Parker, and Peter Parker.
 &nbsp;

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.920
"You're not Peter Parker." 
 
Bringing together three different&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:34.400
Spider-Men makes for a smaller version of the&nbsp;
Spider-Verse to manifest on the big screen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:39.040
It also leaves room for the possibility that other&nbsp;
Spider-Man variants can enter the picture down the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:43.280
road. We know there's plenty of them.
 
"Wherever I go, the wind follows — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:47.760
the wind smells like rain."
 
However, there is one face that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:52.800
fans undoubtedly will expect to show up sooner&nbsp;
rather than later, and that's Miles Morales.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:57.200
He's already led his own flick in the animated&nbsp;
hit "Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse," which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:01.760
will soon have a pair of sequels to its name.&nbsp;
So when will he make the leap to live-action?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:06.400
If a certain "No Way Home" Easter egg is any&nbsp;
indication, it could be right around the corner.
 &nbsp;

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:09.440
"They're starting to come&nbsp;
through, and I can't stop them."

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.000
Miles Morales may not physically appear in&nbsp;
"Spider-Man: No Way Home," but it's made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:18.080
abundantly clear that audiences aren't&nbsp;
the only ones expecting him to pop up.&nbsp;

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:22.240
At the end of the climactic battle, Andrew&nbsp;
Garfield's Peter Parker reveals his face&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:27.840
to his Amazing Spider-Man 2 nemesis, Electro.
After the unmasking, Electro seems disappointed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.400
remarking that because the hero was from Queens,&nbsp;
had a cool costume, and always helped out poor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:38.160
people, he was expecting Spider-Man to be Black.
Electro's surprise shouldn't be too, er, shocking,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:42.000
because the villain has never seen the face&nbsp;
of his nemesis before this interaction.&nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.680
It's a humorous moment, but fans of the&nbsp;
comic books or "Into the Spider-Verse"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:49.200
know there's more to this line than meets&nbsp;
the eye. There is, of course, at least one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:54.080
Black Spider-Man -- Miles Morales -- and while he&nbsp;
hasn't appeared in the MCU yet as a live-action&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:58.640
hero, it's clear the seeds are being planted&nbsp;
for him to show up at some point in the future.&nbsp;

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:02.240
This is far from the first time&nbsp;
Miles has been referenced in the MCU.&nbsp;

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:06.320
In "Spider-Man: Homecoming," Tom Holland's&nbsp;
Spider-Man meets Aaron Davis, who is Miles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:11.360
Morales' uncle within the Marvel canon. (He and&nbsp;
his alter-ego the Prowler previously appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.360 --> 00:02:15.680
outside of the MCU in "Into the Spider-Verse.")
At one point during their "Homecoming"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:20.000
interaction, Aaron even mentions having a&nbsp;
nephew – though he doesn't mention him by name.
 &nbsp;

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:24.960
"The other night, you told that dude, 'If you're&nbsp;
gonna shoot somebody, shoot me.' That's pretty&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:28.960
ballsy. I don't want those weapons in this&nbsp;
neighborhood. I got a nephew who live here."
 &nbsp;

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:34.080
Hopefully, the next time the Spider-Verse comes&nbsp;
into play in the MCU, Miles can get in on the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.920
action. With another MCU "Spider-Man"&nbsp;
trilogy on the way, there's more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:43.280
enough room for another Spidey in this universe.
 
"I thought I was the only one. You're like me."
 &nbsp;

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:47.120
"I don't want to be."
 
"I don't think you have a choice, kiddo."
 &nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.680
As we wait for Miles Morales to make his&nbsp;
way into the MCU, some are wondering:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:56.640
is there another way we might see Tom Holland's&nbsp;
Peter Parker take on Miles as a protege? Maybe!&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.120
In an interview with SyFy Wire, Tom Holland&nbsp;
was asked if he would ever consider joining the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:04.880
animated "Into the Spider-Verse" franchise.
His response was clear:&nbsp;

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:06.960
"Love them, and I'm just&nbsp;
waiting for the phone call."&nbsp;

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:11.200
While it may seem like a pipe dream to get&nbsp;
an MCU star into a purely Sony project,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.960
Holland revealed that there have been talks&nbsp;
behind the scenes about getting him into the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:20.080
Spider-Verse one way or another. He revealed,
"[Spider-Verse producer] Amy [Pascal] actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:23.200
asked me on the set of this movie,&nbsp;
and no one has come back to me."&nbsp;

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:28.320
Could such a cameo end up in the upcoming "Across&nbsp;
the Spider-Verse (Part One)" or "Two?" Perhaps!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.320 --> 00:03:33.040
Judging from the trailer, Miles Morales actually&nbsp;
steps outside of his own reality this time around,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.400
travelling through worlds beyond his&nbsp;
own. It's possible Miles could enter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:41.040
a live-action sphere at some point, briefly&nbsp;
meeting Tom Holland's variant to say, "Hello."&nbsp;

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:45.200
Or perhaps Tom Holland's Spider-Man will&nbsp;
enter Miles's reality and become animated for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.320
a brief period of time. However it transpires,&nbsp;
Electro's wish has already come true: there is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:54.480
a Black Spider-Man, and he'll be web-slinging&nbsp;
his way onto your screens for years to come.
